        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758269,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Commodore 64, affectionately known as the C64, was an 8-bit home computer released in 1982 that became a cultural icon and the best-selling desktop computer of all time, with estimated sales between 12.5 and 17 million units. Boasting 64 kilobytes of RAM and impressive graphics and sound capabilities thanks to its VIC-II chip and SID sound chip, the C64 offered a significant leap in performance compared to its predecessors. It initially sold for $595, but its price later dropped, making it accessible to a wider audience.\n\nThe C64 dominated the home computer market throughout the 1980s, particularly in the US and UK, though it faced stiff competition from the ZX Spectrum and Amstrad CPC. Popular games like *Impossible Mission*, *The Last Ninja*, and *Elite* showcased its capabilities and cemented its legacy. Even today, emulators allow enthusiasts to relive the C64 experience."
          },
